<title>UK: ICO coffee exports down at 5.46 mln bags in August.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports down at 5.46 mln bags in August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Coffee Organisation (ICO) exporting members exports fell to 5.46 million 60-kg bags from 5.79 million in July and 5.92 million in August 1995, ICO figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the 12 months to August 1996 total exports by exporting members to all destinations were up at 70.89 million bags from 65.11 million in the same 1994/95 period.</p>
<p>In the first 11 months of the current coffee year to end-August total exports were up at 65.09 million bags from 59.23 million in the same 1994/95 period, the ICO said.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		  Aug 96     Aug 95     Oct/Aug 96   Oct/Aug 95</p>
<p>TOTAL	   5,460	5,918	65,092	 59,234</p>
<p>Brazil	  1,703	1,381	11,249	 15,025</p>
<p>Colombia	  751	  822	10,083	  8,631</p>
<p>Guatemala	 157	  318	 3,606	  3,281</p>
<p>Mexico	    146	  184	 4,489	  3,155</p>
<p>Indonesia	 646	  647	 4,443	  2,641</p>
<p>Ivory Coast     205	  187	 2,423	  2,037</p>
<p>Uganda	    338	  274	 3,832	  2,508</p>
<p>Vietnam	    76	  241	 3,409	  2,982</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
</text>
